# Bilbo, Thief in the Night: "you may cast ... from your graveyard". The trigger does not ask for mana first, so a player
# who cannot pay finds out while casting and gives the cast up (CR 733.1, 601.2): the spell goes back where it was. On
# turn 5 Bot1 taps its Mountain and Island for mana in the first main phase, and the mana is gone by the time Bilbo
# attacks. Bot1 chooses the Lightning Bolt, names its target, finds {R} unpayable and cancels: the Bolt is still in the
# graveyard (not exiled, not on the stack) and Bot2 has taken only Bilbo's combat damage. The control is
# bilbo-recasts-a-bolt-from-the-graveyard-and-exiles-it, where the Mountain is untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Bilbo, Thief in the Night
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bilbo, Thief in the Night.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Attack(Bilbo, Thief in the Night)
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Cancel
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Exile.Count = 0
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 15
